---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Run a Compose setup in a local Antithesis simulation environment

This command is gated behind the 'simulate' unstable feature. Enable it with
SNOUTY_UNSTABLE_FEATURES=simulate.

After the simulation environment boots, it prints a run ID. Open a second
terminal and use `snouty simulate --attach <ID>` to open a shell in it. Leaving
that shell does not stop the simulation.

Accepts a directory containing docker-compose.yaml, as validate does. Kubernetes
configurations are not supported. Workload images must exist in the local
container engine. The simulation environment image defaults to
antithesis-environment in the configured repository, at the version this release
of snouty pins. An --environment-image without a tag or digest gets that
version. No API key is required.

Requires Linux or macOS and QEMU 8.2 or later. Uses 1 CPU and 15000 MiB of
memory by default. Use --memory to lower its memory when the host has less RAM.
The simulation environment uses the host architecture by default. SSH
configuration is private to this run; user configuration is not changed.

Waits for setup_complete before starting test composer on each rollout. After
the composer watch is ready, calls add_entropy with a fresh random seed and
force=true. Repeats every 30 seconds, including after composer completion.
Pauses faults before stack recreation and waits for setup_complete on the next
rollout. Entropy refresh preserves the current fault pause state. Uses the
simulation environment's configure.py to apply --fault-tolerance and
--fault-exclusions before the first rollout. Fault tolerance defaults to
resilient. Omitted fault exclusions keep the simulation environment's setting.
--fault-tolerance none pauses fault injection before Compose starts and prevents
test composer from unpausing it. Other groups unpause fault injection after
setup_complete. TacticsLang does not use this fault configuration. Repeats
rollouts for templates with driver or check commands until interrupted. Checks
test commands after setup_complete. With no commands or only first_ commands,
keeps the stack running. --disable-restart keeps all workloads running after
composer completion. Failed assertions and composer commands do not stop the
simulation, but cause a nonzero exit status when it stops. On interruption,
requests immediate poweroff, waits up to two seconds, then force-kills the VM if
needed and drains the remaining logs. A second interrupt force-kills the VM
immediately.

Boot console logs are hidden unless startup fails or the VM exits unexpectedly.
Text output uses the same vtime, source, and event rendering as `runs logs`.
With --json, emits newline-delimited events annotated with active faults and a
final failure-count summary. The startup timeout does not limit the simulation
duration.

Example:
  snouty simulate ./config

Usage: snouty simulate [OPTIONS] [CONFIG]

Arguments:
  [CONFIG]
          Path to config directory containing docker-compose.yaml

Options:
      --environment-image <ENVIRONMENT_IMAGE>
          Container image of the simulation environment, containing /guest.iso;
          without a tag or digest, uses the pinned version (default:
          REPOSITORY/antithesis-environment)

      --disable-restart
          Keep the stack running after composer completion, with entropy refresh
          and logs

      --fault-tolerance <FAULT_TOLERANCE>
          Which faults to inject, by how much disruption the system must
          survive. `none`: no faults. `resilient`: degraded network links,
          thread pauses, container pauses of up to 10 seconds, CPU throttling
          and clock jitter. `high_availability`: everything in `resilient`, plus
          network partitions and killed or stopped containers. `legacy`: all
          network faults and thread pausing
          
          [default: resilient]
          [possible values: none, resilient, high_availability, legacy]

      --fault-exclusions <FAULT_EXCLUSIONS>
          Containers that faults must leave alone, matched by name with a Rust
          regex. Thread pausing still applies. Max 1024 characters

      --memory <MEMORY>
          Simulation environment memory in MiB (maximum: 15000)
          
          [default: 15000]

      --attach <ID>
          Open a root shell in a running Compose simulation

      --timeout <TIMEOUT>
          Maximum time to wait for simulation environment startup (for example,
          5m or 300s)
          
          [default: 5m]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Print NDJSON: one JSON object per line

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
